From 218e8350709a2001a5eedad57697b2313ee87947 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:12:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06919/11362] [outer-loop] bp35: L6 SOLVED round 10 (codex,
 three actions to spare)

Round-10 gpt-5.6-sol session found the genuinely-different descent
path round 9 called for: the safe route is through the FAR-RIGHT
row-13 opening (columns 7/8), not columns 2/3/4/5 -- all four
independently confirmed lethal across this and prior rounds. Only
row-20 column 4 needs solidifying before the ascent; trimming
unnecessary setup clicks shaved the route down to land the full win
at action 225, three actions before the hard 228-action timer that
has killed every over-long attempt on this game.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() +
replay via a new resolver priority branch, all 5 confirmed level=6,
state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED (the source agent's own
reproduction_verified is honestly false -- budget ran out after the
win).

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: bp35 levels_reproduced 5 -> 6.
reproducible_total_levels 167 -> 168 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
